1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,110
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,110 --> 00:00:03,440
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:08,150
(Episode 9)

5
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:37,910
Mr. Seok Jin, I really have to go.

6
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:39,540
To the restroom?

7
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:40,550
Yes.

8
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:44,050
There's one over there.

9
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:45,580
Can you go by yourself?

10
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:47,650
Yes, I can go by myself.

11
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:49,350
Can you keep an eye on this?

12
00:02:48,510 --> 00:02:50,140
I'm back from the restroom.

13
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:52,540
- Right. Let's go, Mom.
- Sure.

14
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:57,680
Seok Jin.

15
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:00,250
What are you doing here?
We could've taken a taxi.

16
00:03:00,450 --> 00:03:02,050
Why take a taxi when I have my car?

17
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,060
It's nice to see you, Ms. Park.

18
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:08,290
Right. You too.

19
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:10,500
Let's go, Seok Jin.

20
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:46,730
Lee Jung Tae.

21
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:54,710
Ko Eun Seol.

22
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,640
I need to talk to you.

23
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:01,510
Mr. Lee! Lee Jung Tae!

24
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:10,050
Drive!

25
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,560
Lee Jung Tae!

26
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:24,600
- Eun Seol.
- Attorney Seo.

27
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:25,670
Get in. Hurry.

28
00:04:28,270 --> 00:04:29,310
How are you here?

29
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:31,310
I told you
this isn't just your fight.

30
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:44,360
I've set up your home and office
super nicely.

31
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:52,060
Seok Jin.

32
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:53,630
Yes?

33
00:04:54,130 --> 00:04:55,130
Oh, right.

34
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:57,300
What's on your mind?

35
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:58,500
Oh, well...

36
00:04:58,670 --> 00:04:59,940
It's nothing.

37
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:04,810
- Mr. Seok Jin.
- Yes?

38
00:05:04,810 --> 00:05:06,480
I feel uncomfortable.

39
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:08,410
Why? Do you need the restroom again?

40
00:05:09,150 --> 00:05:10,450
It's not that.

41
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:12,650
Then just hang on.
We'll be there soon.

42
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:22,330
- All right. Let's enjoy our tea.
- Thank you.

43
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:24,660
Dad, where's Mom?

44
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:26,600
I heard Seok Jin is here.

45
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:29,830
Goodness. Have you been well?

46
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:32,240
Are you really Seok Jin?

47
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:35,110
My goodness,
look how handsome you've become.

48
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:37,640
You're as beautiful as ever, ma'am.

49
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:41,310
Oh, please. Time has not been kind.
I'm so depressed about it.

50
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:44,050
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.

51
00:05:47,090 --> 00:05:50,320
Is your mother doing any better?

52
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,920
There hasn't been any major change.

53
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:55,060
Oh, dear.

54
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:56,460
Anyway,

55
00:05:56,630 --> 00:05:58,860
how long do you think it'll take
for you to get up to speed?

56
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,170
I asked for the documents
in advance,

57
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:02,600
so I have a pretty good grasp
of things.

58
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:05,440
- Already?
- Really?

59
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:09,310
So what do you think is Cheongma's
biggest problem right now?

60
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,540
Honey, please.

61
00:06:11,010 --> 00:06:13,480
It hasn't even been an hour
since he landed.

62
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,950
What's the rush?

63
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:17,680
What?
You said the company was in crisis.

64
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:20,150
That's why I took a gamble
on bringing in Chief Cha.

65
00:06:20,150 --> 00:06:21,450
So how is this rude?

66
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:26,690
Cheongma's greatest strength was
its excellent quality for the price.

67
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:30,230
The scholarship foundation further
enhanced the brand's credibility.

68
00:06:30,230 --> 00:06:31,230
However,

69
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,600
the failure
of the new product line...

70
00:06:33,970 --> 00:06:36,700
has significantly damaged
that corporate image.

71
00:06:37,970 --> 00:06:38,970
Seok Jin.

72
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:40,810
Go on.

73
00:06:41,510 --> 00:06:43,070
I believe learning from this...

74
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:46,580
and improving our quality
is our top priority right now.

75
00:06:47,010 --> 00:06:48,180
In order to do that,

76
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:51,150
we urgently need to hire
more talented, creative designers.

77
00:06:52,050 --> 00:06:53,550
Everyone on my team
studied overseas.

78
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:54,850
They're very skilled.

79
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,190
On that point,

80
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,160
I completely agree.

81
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,220
Dad!

82
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:02,630
Hae Ra, are things going well
with Assemblyman Oh's son?

83
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:04,700
Gosh. Honey, come on.

84
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:06,960
What could possibly be going well?

85
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:08,200
Things ended a while ago.

86
00:07:08,430 --> 00:07:09,430
What?

87
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:10,740
He's not my type.

88
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:12,470
Kang Hae Ra.

89
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:15,110
All right.
That's enough of the pleasantries.

90
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:17,610
Since you're here,
you should go see your office.

91
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,510
Hae Ra put a lot of thought
into decorating it.

92
00:07:19,910 --> 00:07:21,580
- Should I?
- Let's go.

93
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:24,920
- Sir.
- Right.

94
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,380
- We'll see you around.
- Sure.

95
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:37,360
Why did you suddenly bring up
Assemblyman Oh's son?

96
00:07:37,830 --> 00:07:39,330
You know why.

97
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,030
I'm telling him
not to get his hopes up.

98
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:44,370
I can't believe you.

99
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
What do you think?

100
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,110
Do you like it?

101
00:07:49,470 --> 00:07:50,470
Yes.

102
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:54,210
Don't worry about
Assemblyman Oh's son.

103
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:56,550
Like I said,
I ended things a while ago.

104
00:07:58,680 --> 00:07:59,680
I believe you.

105
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:01,950
Really?

106
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,660
Ms. Joo, come on.

107
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:13,500
You should behave yourself
at the office, Team Leader Kang.

108
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,830
There's no one else here.

109
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:20,540
Well, I'll get going
and let you two catch up.

110
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,180
Congratulations on your promotion,
Chief Cha.

111
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,750
Thank you, Ms. Joo.

112
00:08:32,950 --> 00:08:35,720
Did Team Leader Kang
tell you anything?

113
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:38,660
About how you ended up here, I mean.

114
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:42,330
Well, I believed I got here
through my own hard work.

115
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:44,560
Of course.

116
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:47,570
Your hard work and success
got you this far,

117
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,600
which is why I pulled some strings.

118
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:51,900
What?

119
00:08:52,170 --> 00:08:53,970
I'm not trying to take
all the credit,

120
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:55,510
but I just thought
you should know...

121
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,540
that I have your back.

122
00:09:02,110 --> 00:09:03,110
Why?

123
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:04,720
Is something wrong?

124
00:09:05,550 --> 00:09:06,580
What? No.

125
00:09:07,850 --> 00:09:09,520
Thank you for having my back.

126
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:14,730
Of course.
It's best to keep things pleasant.

127
00:09:15,830 --> 00:09:16,860
I'll see you later then.

128
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,760
Sure.

129
00:09:27,510 --> 00:09:28,540
Seriously?

130
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:37,950
(Taxi)

131
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:48,860
What are you doing?

132
00:09:49,390 --> 00:09:50,390
What do you think?

133
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,460
I have to keep an eye
on Lee Jung Tae.

134
00:09:51,530 --> 00:09:52,830
Eun Seol, wait.

135
00:09:55,430 --> 00:09:56,570
Eun Seol!

136
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:11,550
Eun Seol,
it's dangerous to act alone.

137
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,250
Welcome.

138
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:16,550
- Hello.
- Do you need a room?

139
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:18,520
Actually, that...

140
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,930
The lady will be staying alone.

141
00:10:23,030 --> 00:10:24,900
Don't make excuses later,

142
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:27,130
and just go in together
from the start.

143
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,700
It's nothing to be ashamed of.
All right?

144
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:33,400
I'd like Room 2007.

145
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:35,470
What?

146
00:10:36,270 --> 00:10:37,840
I'm sensitive about numbers,
you see.

147
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:45,420
No. What's there to worry about?
Nothing's wrong.

148
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:47,520
Come on.

149
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,720
It's hot out,

150
00:10:51,490 --> 00:10:55,030
so don't worry about the bill
and turn on the air conditioning.

151
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:05,940
Eun Seol.

152
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:08,040
He isn't likely
to make any moves today.

153
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:10,310
I suppose so.

154
00:11:12,110 --> 00:11:13,910
Are you actually going to wait here?

155
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:16,310
I have to
if I want to tail Lee Jung Tae.

156
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:21,150
But I'm not comfortable
leaving you here by yourself.

157
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,560
We can't exactly
sleep here together, can we?

158
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:27,890
I guess not.

159
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:30,900
You won't even be able to wash up.

160
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:37,700
I'll be fine. You should go.
I'll call you if anything happens.

161
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:39,740
Okay, then.

162
00:11:40,270 --> 00:11:41,370
Be careful.

163
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:43,210
- Sure.
- Okay.

164
00:12:20,510 --> 00:12:22,180
Did you paint this again for me?

165
00:12:22,810 --> 00:12:23,810
Well...

166
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:27,120
I don't have school anymore,
so I've got nothing but time.

167
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:34,730
Getting expelled isn't all bad then.

168
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:35,990
What did you just say?

169
00:12:38,030 --> 00:12:39,060
Nothing. I take it back.

170
00:12:43,330 --> 00:12:45,500
Even after I leave,
I'll never forget you.

171
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:48,610
I'll call you every day, text you,

172
00:12:49,170 --> 00:12:50,470
and email you.

173
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:53,780
I'll never forget you,
so promise me...

174
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:56,480
you won't forget me either.

175
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,250
Promise me, come on.

176
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,390
You promised.

177
00:13:09,860 --> 00:13:11,460
We'll see each other again, okay?

178
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,880
So you were alive after all.

179
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:08,490
I'm hungry.

180
00:14:09,790 --> 00:14:11,590
Sure, Mom. Let's have dinner.

181
00:14:11,990 --> 00:14:13,060
- Okay.
- Let's go.

182
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,070
Here, try this.

183
00:14:24,770 --> 00:14:26,370
Hae Ra sent this over
and said it's good.

184
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:31,610
I don't like Hae Ra.

185
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:36,210
Why don't you like her?
She even sent us delicious food.

186
00:14:36,810 --> 00:14:39,280
I don't know. I just don't like her.

187
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:43,390
Her smile is fake
when she looks at me.

188
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:47,960
What are you talking about?
Don't be like that, Mom.

189
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:50,290
She's going to be
your daughter-in-law soon.

190
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:52,760
My daughter-in-law?

191
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:55,930
Yes, she's the one
I'm going to marry.

192
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:58,800
So please don't hate her
so much, okay?

193
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:02,510
But I still don't like her.

194
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,640
Come on.

195
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:07,810
Just try it.

196
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:27,960
Who called?

197
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:30,790
Lee Jung Tae, ma'am.

198
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:34,230
I thought he was in Vietnam.
Why the sudden call?

199
00:16:35,430 --> 00:16:37,070
He's back in Korea.

200
00:16:38,370 --> 00:16:40,000
He wants to meet. What should I do?

201
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:45,680
Meet with him, see what he wants,
and then report back to me.

202
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,610
Yes, ma'am.

203
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:06,200
What brings you to Korea
out of the blue?

204
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:07,660
I heard you were looking for me.

205
00:17:08,870 --> 00:17:09,870
Me?

206
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:12,240
I don't recall that.

207
00:17:12,370 --> 00:17:13,470
Oh, really?

208
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,770
I guess I was mistaken.

209
00:17:16,170 --> 00:17:17,540
Let's say I buy that for now.

210
00:17:19,840 --> 00:17:22,350
I also heard
Ko Eun Seol is looking for me.

211
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:23,680
Ko Eun Seol too?

212
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:25,420
Darn.

213
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,550
Come on.

214
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:34,090
Let's be honest with each other.

215
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:38,200
Ko Eun Seol came all the way
to the airport looking for me.

216
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:41,570
How did she even know
you were back in the country?

217
00:17:41,630 --> 00:17:44,200
Seriously. I'm not sure how either.

218
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,240
The problem is...

219
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:51,610
it's only a matter of time
before Ko Eun Seol finds me.

220
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:55,910
Or maybe I could just go to her.

221
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,560
Are you threatening me?

222
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:07,560
I thought we settled this
ten years ago.

223
00:18:07,830 --> 00:18:11,500
Please, a lot can happen
in ten years.

224
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:13,200
Isn't it time...

225
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,870
for a renewal on that deal?

226
00:18:16,270 --> 00:18:19,300
Did you seriously just say
our deal has an expiration date?

227
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:49,630
What? Ko Eun Seol showed up
at the airport?

228
00:18:50,570 --> 00:18:51,570
Yes.

229
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:57,540
So what does he want?

230
00:18:58,480 --> 00:18:59,840
In exchange for his silence,

231
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,650
he's demanding 100,000 dollars.

232
00:19:02,810 --> 00:19:05,320
He's claiming
the expiration date has passed.

233
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:09,590
Should I have the guys
take care of him?

234
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:11,590
Smooth things over
and send him on his way.

235
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:13,990
And give him a firm warning.

236
00:19:15,130 --> 00:19:16,560
Yes, I understand.

237
00:19:26,570 --> 00:19:27,740
Have a seat over here.

238
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,110
I'm sorry for asking you
to come to my office.

239
00:19:36,950 --> 00:19:39,080
Not at all.
I'm sorry for taking up your time.

240
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:41,790
So, did you find anything out?

241
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:45,190
This.

242
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:49,490
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

243
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:00,500
(352R 5217)

244
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:04,840
Lee Jung Tae met
with the car's owner.

245
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,680
And you didn't see the owner's face?

246
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:10,080
Unfortunately, no.

247
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,380
But since they met in secret,

248
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:14,890
I'm sure that car belongs to
whoever hired Lee Jung Tae.

249
00:20:15,290 --> 00:20:17,150
Is there any way
to find out who it is?

250
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:21,290
We'll have to try,
since it's our only clue.

251
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:27,500
Leave it to me. I'll look into it.

252
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:29,670
Okay.

253
00:20:35,370 --> 00:20:36,740
You checked out of the motel, right?

254
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:38,110
Of course.

255
00:20:38,710 --> 00:20:40,840
A gosiwon isn't safe either.

256
00:20:41,210 --> 00:20:42,810
Why don't you look
for a studio apartment?

257
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:44,410
I'll figure something out.

258
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,920
You're busy.
You should get back to work.

259
00:20:47,450 --> 00:20:49,020
I'll just wait
for the elevator with you.

260
00:20:56,430 --> 00:20:57,560
Hello, Director Joo.

261
00:20:57,730 --> 00:20:59,230
It's been a while, Team Leader Seo.

262
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:01,930
Eun Seol, get home safe.

263
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,170
I'll be in touch.

264
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:04,500
Sure.

265
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:34,030
I'm so sorry. Are you okay?

266
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,300
Are you all right?

267
00:21:37,730 --> 00:21:38,740
Yes.

268
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,470
Then it's fine.

269
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,040
Excuse me.

270
00:21:45,110 --> 00:21:46,110
Me?

271
00:21:46,310 --> 00:21:48,210
Looks like
I have your phone instead.

272
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,950
Oh, you're right.

273
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:55,220
(My Dearest Dad)

274
00:21:55,290 --> 00:21:57,790
You're getting a call
from "My Dearest Dad."

275
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:00,390
Thank you.

276
00:22:02,990 --> 00:22:03,990
Dad.

277
00:22:04,930 --> 00:22:06,260
How sweet.

278
00:22:17,370 --> 00:22:18,840
I told you we should meet outside.

279
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:22,350
You said Grandma and Eun Guk
were out.

280
00:22:22,650 --> 00:22:23,950
Right. Drink up.

281
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:25,280
Sure.

282
00:22:26,850 --> 00:22:29,250
So, where are you staying?

283
00:22:30,150 --> 00:22:31,150
A gosiwon.

284
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:32,560
A gosiwon, really?

285
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:37,260
I wish I could at least
get you a studio. I'm sorry.

286
00:22:37,530 --> 00:22:38,930
Things are just too tight right now.

287
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:40,330
Don't say that.

288
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:42,230
Dad, just knowing that
you believe in me...

289
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:43,700
is more than I could ask for.

290
00:22:43,930 --> 00:22:46,700
If a parent can't trust
their own child, who can?

291
00:22:49,710 --> 00:22:52,180
By the way,
what's that posted outside?

292
00:22:52,410 --> 00:22:54,380
Do you have to move out
of this house?

293
00:22:54,710 --> 00:22:56,550
Well, it kind of
turned out that way.

294
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:58,620
But you don't need to worry
about that.

295
00:22:58,780 --> 00:23:02,150
So what are you going to do now?

296
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:05,220
I'm going to find the person
who hurt Mom...

297
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:06,760
and make them pay.

298
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:11,390
How could you find the killer
that even the police couldn't catch?

299
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:17,430
What?

300
00:23:17,570 --> 00:23:19,640
Wait, how are you two
getting home together?

301
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:21,340
We ran into each other out front.

302
00:23:21,970 --> 00:23:23,910
What are you doing here again?

303
00:23:24,470 --> 00:23:26,680
Well, I asked her to come.

304
00:23:27,010 --> 00:23:28,480
I'm the one who wanted to come.

305
00:23:28,650 --> 00:23:30,180
Do you think we're a joke?

306
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:32,850
Why do you keep showing up
when we told you not to?

307
00:23:33,950 --> 00:23:35,690
I was just about to leave.

308
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:38,190
Dad, I'll see you around.

309
00:23:38,420 --> 00:23:40,160
Okay. Get home safe, Eun Seol.

310
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:41,930
You take care too, Eun Guk.

311
00:23:55,470 --> 00:23:57,840
Do you really think I did it?

312
00:23:57,840 --> 00:24:00,210
Do you think I killed Mom?

313
00:24:04,380 --> 00:24:05,880
It wasn't me, Eun Guk.

314
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:09,150
It really wasn't me.

315
00:24:10,090 --> 00:24:11,960
How could I do that?

316
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:14,930
How could I do something like that?

317
00:24:14,990 --> 00:24:16,590
The law found you guilty.

318
00:24:16,590 --> 00:24:18,760
And I'm telling you it wasn't me!

319
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:24,130
Why is it so hard for you
to believe me?

320
00:24:25,170 --> 00:24:26,370
Then what should I do?

321
00:24:26,870 --> 00:24:28,640
If I killed myself right here
in front of you,

322
00:24:29,010 --> 00:24:30,440
would you believe me then?

323
00:24:35,750 --> 00:24:37,580
It really wasn't me, Eun Guk.

324
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:42,720
Please, just believe me this once.

325
00:24:44,690 --> 00:24:47,420
While I'm asking nicely,
just take it and leave.

326
00:24:49,430 --> 00:24:51,090
Eun Guk, seriously!

327
00:24:52,530 --> 00:24:54,630
How can you do this to me?

328
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:57,400
Even if the whole world blames me,

329
00:24:57,670 --> 00:24:59,740
you of all people should believe me.

330
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:05,040
No matter what anyone else says,
at least you should believe me.

331
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:19,990
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

332
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:21,060
Yes, Detective Kim.

333
00:25:21,830 --> 00:25:23,260
Did you look into the matter
I asked you about?

334
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:28,600
Oh, really? So who owns the vehicle?

335
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:32,440
It's not privately owned.
It's a Cheongma Group company car.

336
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:35,410
A Cheongma Group company car?

337
00:25:36,370 --> 00:25:37,410
Cheongma Group?

338
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:40,910
Isn't that the company you work for?

339
00:25:41,950 --> 00:25:42,950
That's right.

340
00:25:43,210 --> 00:25:44,450
How on earth...

341
00:25:45,580 --> 00:25:48,520
Then we just need to find out
who that company car is assigned to.

342
00:25:49,550 --> 00:25:51,760
I'm going to check
with General Affairs tomorrow.

343
00:25:52,390 --> 00:25:55,790
So, will we find out who hired
Lee Jung Tae by tomorrow?

344
00:25:57,130 --> 00:25:58,130
That's right.

345
00:26:10,510 --> 00:26:11,510
Excuse me.

346
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:13,640
- Oh, hey.
- Hello.

347
00:26:13,980 --> 00:26:15,650
What brings
the head of the Legal Team here?

348
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:17,180
I dropped by to ask something.

349
00:26:18,010 --> 00:26:19,920
Your department manages
the company cars, right?

350
00:26:20,150 --> 00:26:22,220
Yes, that's right. Why do you ask?

351
00:26:25,090 --> 00:26:27,660
This license plate is from
one of our company cars, isn't it?

352
00:26:28,290 --> 00:26:30,160
Can you check who it's assigned to?

353
00:26:32,360 --> 00:26:33,360
One moment.

354
00:26:36,830 --> 00:26:40,700
(352R 5217: Pool Vehicle)

355
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:43,310
Oh, this car isn't for an executive.

356
00:26:43,670 --> 00:26:45,740
It's a pool car
that all employees share.

357
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,140
A pool car?

358
00:26:47,280 --> 00:26:48,280
Yes.

359
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:52,680
Then can you tell me
who checked out the car this week?

360
00:26:53,420 --> 00:26:54,420
One moment.

361
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:00,690
Team Leader Seo.

362
00:27:03,660 --> 00:27:05,200
Manager Na, hey.

363
00:27:05,330 --> 00:27:07,860
What brings the head of Legal
to General Affairs?

364
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:10,770
The Legal Team
is investigating a matter.

365
00:27:12,270 --> 00:27:16,040
Mr. Seo, there are no records
of it being used at all this week.

366
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:18,710
What? That can't be right.

367
00:27:19,580 --> 00:27:21,610
Then is it possible to take it
without logging the trip?

368
00:27:21,610 --> 00:27:23,210
No way.

369
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:25,150
We manage
all the car keys ourselves.

370
00:27:25,820 --> 00:27:26,850
Is that so?

371
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:28,490
Thank you.

372
00:27:29,620 --> 00:27:30,620
Have a good day.

373
00:27:41,530 --> 00:27:42,530
Right.

374
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:46,570
So, did you make sure to erase
the vehicle usage records?

375
00:27:49,140 --> 00:27:51,040
Good. You did well.

376
00:27:59,420 --> 00:28:01,180
I'm sorry I let you down.

377
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:04,250
Why are you apologizing
when it's not your fault?

378
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:07,360
Deleting the vehicle logs?

379
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:08,930
I really thought
we had the killer this time.

380
00:28:10,030 --> 00:28:11,830
But at least one thing
is certain now.

381
00:28:12,930 --> 00:28:15,830
The person we're after
is inside Cheongma.

382
00:28:20,140 --> 00:28:21,810
If they won't show themselves,

383
00:28:22,570 --> 00:28:24,210
then I'll have to go in myself.

384
00:28:28,180 --> 00:28:29,680
You're going to get into Cheongma?

385
00:28:30,710 --> 00:28:31,710
How?

386
00:28:32,150 --> 00:28:34,320
I'll have to find a way,
no matter what it takes.

387
00:28:35,590 --> 00:28:38,820
I spent ten years in prison
for a crime I didn't commit.

388
00:28:41,190 --> 00:28:42,890
I'm getting into Cheongma,
no matter what.

389
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:49,270
You want to hire a designer
through an open competition?

390
00:28:49,830 --> 00:28:52,070
- Yes.
- Why go through all that trouble?

391
00:28:52,140 --> 00:28:53,640
We can just hire someone
based on their resume.

392
00:28:54,500 --> 00:28:55,910
I want to remove resume bias...

393
00:28:55,910 --> 00:28:57,970
and choose someone
based purely on their work.

394
00:28:58,240 --> 00:28:59,710
I'm going to bring in
outside judges too.

395
00:29:00,140 --> 00:29:01,140
Seok Jin.

396
00:29:02,210 --> 00:29:03,350
It's Chief Cha now.

397
00:29:03,850 --> 00:29:05,010
Do you think you're at home?

398
00:29:05,420 --> 00:29:07,280
How can you not separate business
from your personal life?

399
00:29:08,250 --> 00:29:11,150
Anyway,
I don't think it's necessary.

400
00:29:11,650 --> 00:29:13,760
If it were up to me,
I wouldn't hire anyone else.

401
00:29:13,990 --> 00:29:15,630
If we must hire someone,

402
00:29:15,630 --> 00:29:17,160
I'll go over the resumes
and make a solid choice myself.

403
00:29:17,560 --> 00:29:21,200
Proceed with the competition
and hire the designer.

404
00:29:21,560 --> 00:29:23,330
- Dad!
- Understood.

405
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:24,400
Good.

406
00:29:27,970 --> 00:29:32,910
(Cheongma Group's Open Competition
for New Designers)

407
00:29:36,310 --> 00:29:38,680
(2026 New Designer Competition:
Application Desk)

408
00:29:57,700 --> 00:29:58,800
Well, look who it is.

409
00:30:11,150 --> 00:30:13,420
It really is you, Ko Eun Seol.

410
00:30:15,950 --> 00:30:17,220
Oh, right.

411
00:30:18,320 --> 00:30:19,560
This is your family's company,
isn't it?

412
00:30:54,590 --> 00:30:58,460
(A Trap Called Desire)

413
00:30:58,560 --> 00:31:00,760
So you're saying you need
Cheongma's internal documents.

414
00:31:00,830 --> 00:31:01,860
Can looking at some documents...

415
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,830
really help you win
the designer competition?

416
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:05,400
I hear
you're the head of the Legal Team.

417
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:08,540
I'm Cha Seok Jin,
the new Chief of Planning.

418
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:11,540
Do you want your sister
to be the killer?

419
00:31:11,570 --> 00:31:14,040
Are you afraid to know you hated
your sister for ten years...

420
00:31:14,040 --> 00:31:15,210
for nothing?

421
00:31:15,610 --> 00:31:17,250
Why do you hate me so much?

422
00:31:17,580 --> 00:31:19,750
Because you don't know your place.

423
00:31:20,180 --> 00:31:22,190
Stop getting involved with someone
as rude and arrogant as me,

424
00:31:22,250 --> 00:31:23,890
and just go your own way.

425
00:31:24,220 --> 00:31:26,320
Do you happen to remember
someone named Ko Eun Seol?

426
00:31:26,620 --> 00:31:28,560
A murderer like her? How could she?

427
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:30,290
In her dreams.

428
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:34,130
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
